    <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">cleave <span class="badge badge-stable">stable</span></h2>
    <p>AST-aware software decomposition engine for supply-chain triage.
    Detects capabilities and behaviors across 20+ languages and six binary
    formats in a single pass. Useful as a standalone triage tool, and the
    feature layer beneath <a href="/litmus/">litmus</a>.</p>

    <h2>Capabilities</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>20+ languages</strong> — Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Go, Rust, C/C++, Java, C#, Swift, Objective-C, Ruby, PHP, Perl, Lua, Shell, PowerShell, Groovy, Scala, Zig, Elixir</li>
      <li><strong>Binary formats</strong> — Mach-O, ELF, PE, Java .class, Python .pyc, compiled AppleScript</li>
      <li><strong>Archive formats</strong> — ZIP, TAR, 7z, RAR, plus JAR/WAR, deb, rpm, apk, gem, crate, whl, nupkg, phar, vsix, xpi, crx, ipa, epub</li>
      <li><strong>Document &amp; data formats</strong> — RTF, LNK, PNG steganography, PDF, plist, VBScript, Batch, manifests, GitHub Actions workflows</li>
      <li><strong>AST traversal</strong> via Tree-sitter for source-level analysis</li>
      <li><strong>Binary reverse engineering</strong> via Rizin, header parsing via Goblin</li>
      <li><strong>Signature matching</strong> via YARA-X</li>
      <li><strong>String extraction</strong> via <a href="/stng/">stng</a> for payload decoding</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI-derived rulesets</h2>
    <p>Cleave's rulesets blend hand-curated detectors with AI-derived ones.
    The hand-curated rules give precision for well-known patterns; the
    AI-derived rules — drawn from a training corpus of over a million
    samples — give breadth across 20+ languages and six binary formats
    that no team could maintain alone.</p>
    <p>The AI lives in the build pipeline, not the runtime. Once shipped,
    cleave is deterministic: same input, same output, every run. No model
    weights at execution time, no GPU, no network calls, no telemetry.</p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
Homebrew (macOS or Linux):

<pre class="install-block">
brew tap atomdrift/tap https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/homebrew-tap.git

brew install atomdrift/tap/cleave
</pre>

From source

<pre class="install-block">
git clone --depth 1 https://codeberg.org/atomdrift/cleave.git
make install
</pre>

    <h2>Usage</h2>
    <pre class="install-block">$ cleave suspect.bin
$ cleave /tmp/box-o-malware   # recursive, unpacks archives</pre>

    <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.8125rem;">For more thorough results, install
    <a href="https://github.com/rizinorg/rizin" target="_blank">Rizin</a> (binary reverse-engineering) and
    <a href="https://github.com/upx/upx" target="_blank">UPX</a> (unpacker).</p>

